# Tether Link Utility

> Tether Link Utility is an Android app that shares a phone's mobile data with your laptop, tablet or another phone through a local SOCKS5 proxy shared over the phone's Wi-Fi hotspot. No root, no account, no remote server.

## What it does
- Runs entirely on-device: no remote server, no account required.
- Uses Android's VpnService API to run a local SOCKS5 proxy on the phone; connected devices send their traffic to that proxy and the phone forwards it over its mobile data connection.
- Free tier: 1 device at a time, with ads. Pro (paid): up to 5 devices at once, no ads.
- Works with Windows, macOS, Linux, Android, and iOS clients. Windows and Mac (recommended): a small setup file (https://tetherlinkutility.com/downloads/TLU-Windows-Setup.cmd) or script (https://tetherlinkutility.com/downloads/tlu-mac-tunnel.zip) installs and runs sing-box in TUN mode for you, so every app on the computer, DNS included, uses the phone's connection. iPhone: the free Potatso app. Linux: sing-box, or Firefox for the browser only.
- Android-to-Android connections are simplified via QR code scanning (usually one tap, no manual Wi-Fi setup).
- Connecting another device: after START SHARING the app asks which device will connect (Android, Windows, iPhone, Mac, Linux, or Other such as a TV or game console), then, for a Windows PC or a Mac, shows the setup file or script to download first; for other devices it asks whether they already have the app they need (Tether Link Utility on Android, Potatso on iPhone, Firefox on Linux) before showing any Wi-Fi details. It shows how to install without internet (Android: Play Store app sharing; Windows: download the setup file on the phone and send it by Bluetooth or USB cable), then one connect screen that waits until the device connects, and a "Still not connected?" list sorted by what the user sees.
- Browser-only option (Windows, Linux): Firefox, Settings, type "proxy" in the search box, Configure proxy, Manual proxy configuration, SOCKS Host and Port, SOCKS v5, tick "Proxy DNS when using SOCKS v5", OK. Only that browser uses the phone's connection; the setup file or sing-box covers every app.
- How-to videos: Windows https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Qn6gi9P8fSs , Mac https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wj4suAZMxSQ . Written steps: https://tetherlinkutility.com/blog/socks5-proxy-setup-windows-macos-ios.html#windows
- Data used by connected devices counts toward the phone's mobile plan; users should check their carrier's terms for tethering.

## Key facts
- Platform: Android app (the server/host device must be Android). Client devices can be Windows, macOS, Android, or iOS.
- Price: free to install and use with a 1-device limit and ads; Pro is from $3.99/month (exact price shown in the store; varies by country and platform) and removes ads and raises the device limit to 5. See https://tetherlinkutility.com/pricing.md
- Speed: actual speed depends on the carrier, plan and signal.
- Not a VPN or privacy service: it does not encrypt traffic or route it through any third-party server. All routing happens locally on the device.
- Privacy: routed traffic is never sent to our servers or logged by the proxy. The free version shows Google AdMob ads, and the ad provider may collect device identifiers. The app also uses Firebase Analytics, Crashlytics and Remote Config. The privacy policy explains the data types and how to request deletion.

